# The soak candidate: the commit the scheduled certification run certifies.
#
# **What it is for.** The layer exits on five consecutive qualifying runs of
# `.github/workflows/certify.yml` over one frozen candidate. A run that took the
# default branch's head would mint a new candidate on every merge, and the count
# would then be held by nobody merging — a discipline no file records and no run
# attests. So the candidate is pinned here.
#
# **How it is reached.** `.github/workflows/soak.yml` on the default branch
# holds the nightly cron and nothing else a run does. It reads this file, fetches
# the commit, checks that the tree at it carries `certify.yml`, computes the
# suite-manifest digest there, tags the commit `soak-candidate/<sha>` and
# dispatches `certify.yml` **at that tag**. The certification run is therefore
# one tree: its steps and its suites are both the candidate's, and `GITHUB_SHA`
# is the pin. Anything the dispatcher cannot verify ends the dispatcher red and
# starts no run.
#
# **Editing it starts a new count.** That is the whole point of the edit, and it
# is a reviewed commit like any other. Nothing here retires the records already
# written: they name the candidate they ran, so a campaign reading them sees the
# candidate change rather than inheriting it.
#
# **The candidate is advanced by a reviewed commit after the mechanism merges.**
# A pin can only name a commit that already exists, so the commit introducing
# this file cannot name itself. The sha below is therefore this mechanism's
# base, which carries no `certify.yml` — the first dispatch after the merge
# refuses it by name and dispatches nothing, until somebody advances the pointer
# to a commit that carries the mechanism. That refusal is loud, is a failure of
# the dispatcher rather than of a certification run, and is the designed state
# of this file between the merge and the first pointer advance.
#
# **Format.** `#` comments, then one line holding a 40-digit lowercase commit
# sha. `.github/scripts/soak-candidate.sh` is the one parser; the same shape is
# asserted by `norn --test certification`, so a pull request meets it before
# 04:00 does.
#
# This file is outside the trees the suite manifest sweeps: what the suite is
# and which commit it is run against are two values, and folding the pointer
# into the first would restart the count every time the second advanced.
